{
  "schema": 24,
  "id": "boss-bd2",
  "name": "Boss BD-2 Blues Driver",
  "version": {
    "major": 1,
    "minor": 0
  },
  "description": "Boss BD-2 Blues Driver (1995), drawn from Boss's service schematic (the BD-2 MT board), with Boss's part numbers: a JFET input buffer, two discrete op-amps (a JFET pair and a PNP each) sharing the dual Drive pot, 1SS133 diodes clipping to ground between them, the tone network, Tone and Volume, an M5218 stage with its bass boost, and an emitter-follower output buffer. Boss's JFET switching, its flip-flop and the LED aren't drawn: the switching JFETs are closed (effect on). The 2SK184-GR, 2SC2458, 2SC2459 and M5218AL are our own cards from Toshiba's and Mitsubishi's sheets; the 2SA1335s are 2N3906s, as Aion's Sapphire has them.",
  "tags": [
    "overdrive"
  ],
  "starter": true,
