  "notes": {
    "part:D2": "Reverse-polarity protection: a shunt across the supply, as on the Boss board (a 1N4001 standing in; its part number can't be read on Boss's scan; the 2009 board has a 1N4004, and the 1N4001 card stands in for it: one sheet covers both, differing only in voltage rating).",
    "part:Q2": "Ripple filter: R6 and C4 smooth Q2's base, its emitter follows as VA (Boss's +8V).",
    "part:IC1A": "Buffers VB (Boss's +4V), half of VA (R5, R4), the bias for every stage.",
    "part:Q3": "Input buffer (source follower), biased at VB by R15.",
    "part:C15": "C15, C18 and the 100k resistors R17 and R22 are where Boss's input switch (Q6) sits; with the effect on it conducts, so it's drawn as a wire.",
    "part:Q10": "Q10 and Q11 are a JFET differential pair; with Q9 they make a discrete op-amp. Q10's gate is the + input, Q11's the − input.",
    "part:VR1A": "Drive, first stage's gang of the dual 250kA pot: the stage's gain is about 1 + (R29 + VR1A) / R31.",
    "part:VR1B": "Drive, second stage's gang: about 1 + (R27 + VR1B) / R34.",
    "part:C22": "With R31, sets the first stage's gain and its bass cut (no gain at DC, so the stage stays biased at VB).",
    "part:R37": "R37 with C26, and R38, C34, C35 with R50 and R51, shape the signal into the clipping diodes: they pass the highs and trim the bass.",
    "part:D7": "Two diodes in series each way to ground (D7-D10): the signal clips at about ±1.2 V between the stages.",
    "part:C19": "With R26 a fixed treble cut; C17 across R26 lets some highs through.",
    "part:VR2": "Tone: a passive treble cut.",
    "part:IC1B": "Bass boost: Q7 with C9, C16 and R21 is a gyrator (a simulated inductor) in the feedback; the stage lifts the low end. D1 and D3 clip softly between its inputs on loud peaks.",
    "part:C7": "C7, C6 and the 100k resistors R11 and R8 are where Boss's effect switch (Q4) sits, drawn closed.",
    "part:Q1": "Output buffer (emitter follower).",
    "net:clip": "After the first stage's clipping diodes, on to the second stage through C27."
  },
